Double-click the file **Task 3.html** (or open the browser and use **File > Open file**) to see the page. What the page shows:

- a scrolling line (the `<marquee>` tag) in blue: **COMPUTER SCIENCE IS GOOD**, and a second underlined line **THIS IS GROUP THREE**;
- a thick horizontal line (`<hr size=6>`);
- the bold, underlined sentence **I would love to read the following subjects at the Advanced Level:** followed by a **bulleted list** in italics (computer Science, Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics);
- another thick horizontal line;
- the bold, underlined sentence **My friend Peter would like to read at the Advanced Level:** followed by a **numbered list** in italics: 1. French Language, 2. Literature in English, 3. History.

(`<marquee>` and `<font>` are old tags, no longer part of the standard, but the common browsers still display them.)
